WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.750
(exciting music)

00:00:04.629 --> 00:00:05.997
- So we are here in Singapore.

00:00:05.997 --> 00:00:07.704
It's 10:30 right now.

00:00:07.704 --> 00:00:09.645
Annie really wanted
breakfast this morning.

00:00:09.645 --> 00:00:11.352
- I also already ate breakfast.

00:00:11.352 --> 00:00:12.325
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:12.325 --> 00:00:13.728
Wait, seriously?
- You did?

00:00:13.728 --> 00:00:14.681
- Yeah.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:15.628
- Where are we right now?

00:00:15.628 --> 00:00:17.376
- We are at Ghum Moh Road Market Center,

00:00:17.376 --> 00:00:18.514
one of the best hawker centers.

00:00:18.514 --> 00:00:19.712
Hawker center is just a bunch

00:00:19.712 --> 00:00:21.936
of really, really good food stalls.

00:00:21.936 --> 00:00:23.269
- All right, let's go eat.

00:00:23.269 --> 00:00:24.216
Are you going to help us order?

00:00:24.216 --> 00:00:25.169
- Yeah, sure.

00:00:25.169 --> 00:00:26.137
- Yo, Singaporean dollar.

00:00:26.137 --> 00:00:27.408
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:27.408 --> 00:00:28.325
The 50, 10.

00:00:31.494 --> 00:00:32.327
That one.

00:00:32.327 --> 00:00:35.561
Yo, this dish is so much Chee Cheong Fun.

00:00:35.561 --> 00:00:36.604
- Chee Cheong Fun, all right.

00:00:36.604 --> 00:00:38.482
(electronic music)

00:00:38.482 --> 00:00:39.832
- Next, next!
- Next!

00:00:39.832 --> 00:00:42.431
This is the carrot cake stall.

00:00:42.431 --> 00:00:43.636
There's like a black version

00:00:43.636 --> 00:00:45.168
and there's the white version,

00:00:45.168 --> 00:00:46.562
and then we gotta get both.

00:00:46.562 --> 00:00:47.922
Because it tastes different.

00:00:47.922 --> 00:00:49.561
- This is $2.50.

00:00:49.561 --> 00:00:52.170
This is the hidden luxury of Singapore.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.112
- We're running out of hands.
- Want to put it down?

00:00:54.112 --> 00:00:55.537
We're going to put the food down.

00:00:55.537 --> 00:00:56.386
There's too much food already.

00:00:56.386 --> 00:00:57.784
There is a service

00:00:57.784 --> 00:01:00.844
that delivers hawker food to your office.

00:01:00.844 --> 00:01:03.424
Can they deliver to BuzzFeed?

00:01:03.424 --> 00:01:06.438
- Appam.
- Can we get Appam?

00:01:06.438 --> 00:01:09.355
(electronic music)

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:14.580
- Wait, whoa whoa whoa.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:15.428
What is this?

00:01:15.428 --> 00:01:17.097
- So this is green apple with yakult.

00:01:17.097 --> 00:01:18.488
- This is my friend Ryan.

00:01:18.488 --> 00:01:21.821
They make food videos here in Singapore.

00:01:24.862 --> 00:01:26.610
- Last food.
- Where?

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:27.443
- You guys ready?
- Yes.

00:01:27.443 --> 00:01:28.674
- We're going to get Malay food.

00:01:28.674 --> 00:01:30.699
Mee Siam.
- Haha.

00:01:30.699 --> 00:01:31.948
The best food.

00:01:31.948 --> 00:01:34.865
(electronic music)

00:01:41.536 --> 00:01:43.357
- All right, what should we eat first?

00:01:43.357 --> 00:01:45.075
Let's have some fun.

00:01:45.075 --> 00:01:47.387
This is rice cake with sesame seeds on top

00:01:47.387 --> 00:01:51.779
and then the sauce looks like
it's some sort of sweet ...

00:01:51.779 --> 00:01:53.837
- It's very satisfying to just poke.

00:01:53.837 --> 00:01:54.871
- You already eat?
- No!

00:01:54.871 --> 00:01:56.943
- Why are you chewing?

00:01:56.943 --> 00:01:59.349
Breakfast!

00:01:59.349 --> 00:02:01.795
- It's just savory Jell-o.
- That's Jell-o.

00:02:01.795 --> 00:02:02.780
- Doesn't it like melt in your mouth?

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:04.427
- It's also a nice spice.

00:02:04.427 --> 00:02:07.198
- It's almost like I'm
drinking it, it's so good.

00:02:07.198 --> 00:02:08.987
That's the good stuff, you know?

00:02:08.987 --> 00:02:10.823
When you don't have to
work to eat your food--

00:02:10.823 --> 00:02:12.405
- Yeah, it can just go down your gullet.

00:02:12.405 --> 00:02:14.853
(mellow jazz)

00:02:14.853 --> 00:02:16.757
- It's the same radish and stuff,

00:02:16.757 --> 00:02:18.507
but like in terms of
taste, it's not the same.

00:02:18.507 --> 00:02:20.507
- Egg, radish, scallion,

00:02:22.061 --> 00:02:26.295
and it's all fried together
like almost like a fried rice.

00:02:26.295 --> 00:02:27.201
We've got birds hanging out

00:02:27.201 --> 00:02:29.534
over there.
- Shut up, birds.

00:02:32.057 --> 00:02:32.913
- All right, Alex.

00:02:32.913 --> 00:02:34.203
I think you've got enough bird footage.

00:02:34.203 --> 00:02:35.052
- What is this?

00:02:35.052 --> 00:02:36.041
- Radish.
- Radish.

00:02:36.041 --> 00:02:36.874
- Oh.

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:40.188
- I don't think there was carrot in there.

00:02:40.188 --> 00:02:41.541
- No.

00:02:41.541 --> 00:02:43.140
Cheers.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.038
It's just like fried rice.

00:02:44.038 --> 00:02:46.164
It's like hearty, soulful.

00:02:46.164 --> 00:02:47.914
I want to eat this every morning.

00:02:47.914 --> 00:02:50.076
Okay, so it's exactly the same
thing but different sauce.

00:02:50.076 --> 00:02:50.909
- Yeah.

00:02:50.909 --> 00:02:52.732
Which one do you prefer?
- This one.

00:02:52.732 --> 00:02:54.160
- What?
- It's so sweet.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:55.226
It's still salty.

00:02:55.226 --> 00:02:56.694
It's just like a step-up.

00:02:56.694 --> 00:02:58.666
- A theme that we're having
is everything is very soft.

00:02:58.666 --> 00:03:01.653
(down-tempo music)

00:03:01.653 --> 00:03:03.806
- [Annie] You've got to stir it first.

00:03:03.806 --> 00:03:05.066
- All right Annie, don't eat yet.

00:03:05.066 --> 00:03:06.204
Cheers.
- Cheers.

00:03:06.204 --> 00:03:08.904
- I've never had that kind
of noodle consistency.

00:03:08.904 --> 00:03:10.436
- Where have you been?
- Yeah.

00:03:10.436 --> 00:03:11.748
- I don't know.
- I love

00:03:11.748 --> 00:03:15.094
Malaysian style curries
because they are milder.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:17.578
You can just drink up all of it,

00:03:17.578 --> 00:03:19.092
but it's also light so it doesn't

00:03:19.092 --> 00:03:20.344
fill your stomach up too much.

00:03:20.344 --> 00:03:22.084
- We call it like, "very shiok."

00:03:22.084 --> 00:03:23.612
You know what that means?
- I'm shook!

00:03:23.612 --> 00:03:24.445
- You're shook?
- Shiok.

00:03:24.445 --> 00:03:25.708
It's like so good that you just say like,

00:03:25.708 --> 00:03:27.476
"Oh my gosh. This is so shiok."

00:03:27.476 --> 00:03:30.059
(mellow music)

00:03:31.203 --> 00:03:32.372
- It's like an Indian pancake.
- It's beautiful.

00:03:32.372 --> 00:03:33.478
It was rice and coconut.

00:03:33.478 --> 00:03:35.011
Which one?
- Oh!

00:03:35.011 --> 00:03:36.213
- What should we eat with?

00:03:36.213 --> 00:03:38.003
Mine goes straight to this.

00:03:38.003 --> 00:03:38.836
What is it?

00:03:38.836 --> 00:03:40.124
- Curry.
- Curry.

00:03:40.124 --> 00:03:41.144
This one is sugar and coconut.

00:03:41.144 --> 00:03:42.146
- Whoa!
- Oh, my Gosh.

00:03:42.146 --> 00:03:44.202
- Orange sugar?

00:03:44.202 --> 00:03:47.128
- It's almost like a crepe.

00:03:47.128 --> 00:03:48.792
- The point of this is
to absorb the flavors

00:03:48.792 --> 00:03:49.676
of whatever you pick, right?
- Uh huh.

00:03:49.676 --> 00:03:51.512
- The sugar is really good.

00:03:51.512 --> 00:03:52.478
It's my favorite.

00:03:52.478 --> 00:03:53.588
- Why is it in an orange?

00:03:53.588 --> 00:03:55.252
That's for a child.

00:03:55.252 --> 00:03:57.292
That's like, straight up sugar!

00:03:57.292 --> 00:03:58.617
It's like cotton candy!

00:03:58.617 --> 00:04:00.621
- Mmm, it's so good.
- So good, right?

00:04:00.621 --> 00:04:02.224
- The outside is really crispy.

00:04:02.224 --> 00:04:03.072
It's like a crepe

00:04:03.072 --> 00:04:04.722
and the inside is more
like a doughy bread.

00:04:04.722 --> 00:04:07.306
I gotta say that the curry
is the way to go here.

00:04:07.306 --> 00:04:08.716
- Sugar.
- Team Sugar!

00:04:08.716 --> 00:04:09.872
- Team Spice, baby.

00:04:09.872 --> 00:04:10.976
- I want to go to sleep.

00:04:10.976 --> 00:04:12.968
- I got shiok.
- Shiok.

00:04:12.968 --> 00:04:13.816
- I'm shook.

00:04:13.816 --> 00:04:15.816
Wait, how do you say it?

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:21.507
Alex, you should try some.

00:04:25.236 --> 00:04:26.223
- [Annie] Not shook.

00:04:26.223 --> 00:04:27.056
It's "Shiok."

00:04:27.056 --> 00:04:27.889
- I-o-k.

00:04:27.889 --> 00:04:30.389
- S-H-I-O-K.

00:04:32.204 --> 00:04:33.525
- Shiok.
- Shiok.

00:04:33.525 --> 00:04:34.752
- Maybe "shook" and "shock".

00:04:34.752 --> 00:04:35.994
- It's like "shocked"
and "shook" together?

00:04:35.994 --> 00:04:36.896
Is that what you just said?

00:04:36.896 --> 00:04:37.744
- [Annie] Shiok.

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:39.244
It was very shiok.

